    },
    "done_when": "Reading only /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/101154.zarr (read-only), a script under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/jtmm-flux-loop-correspondence run in place on the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set) with the main checkout's environment (/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv/bin/python) relates each of the 34 PSRC channels magFluxLp1 to magFluxLp34 to the 34 MDAC channels magFlxLp1 to magFlxLp34. Each pair is put on the PSRC channel's time base over their common time window, and two relations are fitted by least squares: PSRC = a * MDAC + b, and PSRC = a * (cumulative time integral of MDAC) + b, in case the raw channel carries a voltage. For each PSRC channel it records the best MDAC channel, which relation, a, b, the residual relative to the PSRC channel's range, and the ratio of the runner-up's residual to the best. Units come from each array's units attribute. The script, its log and the full table as JSON land in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/jtmm-flux-loop-correspondence. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-flux-loop-correspondence.html carries the 34-row table and names every PSRC channel whose best match is not unique (runner-up ratio below 2) or whose relative residual exceeds 5 percent, and states plainly whether the correspondence is the identity permutation. It must not guess positions: which geo.in loop each channel is stays with SELENE's getseldata index. This node never writes under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa and never contacts the JT-60SA server (no ssh jt-60sa, no EDDB call).",
    "estimated_hours": 1.0,
